The 6 Core Code Files to Study
Comprehensive educational study comments have been added directly to these files. You can open and read through them directly in IntelliJ.

1.

SlotCalculationService.java
What it is: The core slot calculation algorithm engine.
How it works:
Fixed 45-min Matrix: Divides the salon operating day (08:15 to 22:30) into twenty 45-minute slots.
Past Slot Filtering: If the requested date is today, slots prior to the current local time are tagged as "Passed".
$O(1)$ Hash Set Checks: Loads active bookings and barber breaks for the day and indexes them as chairId_slotTime keys (e.g., "chair_1_10:30").
Specific vs. "ANY" Chair:
Specific chair: Checks if that single chair is booked or on break.
"ANY" chair: Scans both chairs; if at least one chair is free, marks "Open" and assigns the available chair.
2.

BookingService.java
What it is: The customer reservation pipeline.
How it works:
Chair Resolution: If the customer selects "ANY", it load-balances by finding the first chair unoccupied for that slot.
Double-Booking Guard: Uses @Transactional and checks the database before inserting to prevent race conditions when two users attempt the same slot simultaneously.
Pricing & Duration: Calculates totals from selected catalog services.
OTP & Ticket Generation: Produces a 4-digit verification code (e.g. 4821) and ticket number (GS-XXXX).
Live Queue Position: Counts all pending appointments preceding this customer on the assigned chair.
3.

QueueManagementService.java
What it is: The operational heartbeat for the Barber Workstation.
How it works:
Live Chair Countdown: Calculates elapsedSeconds and remainingSeconds using Duration.between(startedAt, now).
OTP Verification (verifyOtp): Changes status from PENDING → SEATED and records startedAt = LocalDateTime.now().
Service Completion (completeService): Changes status to COMPLETED, records completedAt, and calls

WalletService.deductCommission(salonId, 50.0)
.
Express Walk-Ins (registerWalkIn): Issues WI-XXX tickets. If the chair is free, the customer is seated immediately; otherwise queued.
Cascading Delay Shifts (applyDelayShift): Moves downstream pending appointments forward by +15 minutes if a cut runs over.
4.

PublicBookingController.java
What it is: The REST API gateway for the Customer mobile/web frontend (/api/v1/public).
Key Endpoints to Inspect:
GET /salons/{id}/slots: Calls

SlotCalculationService
.
POST /bookings: Calls

BookingService.createBooking
.
GET /bookings/{id}/pass: Returns the live digital queue pass for ticket polling.
5.

BarberController.java
What it is: The REST API gateway for the Barber Tablet interface (/api/v1/barber).
Key Endpoints to Inspect:
GET /workstation/{salonId}: Returns current chairs, active customer countdown timers, upcoming queues, telemetry stats, and wallet balance.
POST /verify-otp: Validates the customer's arrival code.
POST /complete-service/{id}: Completes haircut and charges platform commission.
POST /delay-shift: Adds +15 mins to downstream customer estimates.
6.

Appointment.java
What it is: The core JPA database entity mapped to the appointments SQL table.
Key Fields:
ticketNumber: GS-1042 or WI-105
otp: 4-digit code
status:

AppointmentStatus
 (PENDING → SEATED → COMPLETED)
startedAt & completedAt: Timestamps driving the barber's active countdown timer.
